    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "An in-situ permeability experiment in rock salt is simulated with METROPOL-2, a model for ground water flow designed by the National Institute of Public Health and Environmental Protection (RIVM), to validate the model for flow in low-permeability rocks. This is done in the framework of INTRAVAL, a project concerned with the validation of mathematical transport models of radioactive substances into the geosphere. The first pulse of the pressure build up experiment in bore hole S0P01 of the Waste Isolation Pilot Plant is simulated accurately with METROPOL.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
